#
# A 4x4 grid of ASICs split into two hosts by column. The square shape is the point: a [2,1]
# host_topology and a [1,2] one describe the same partition up to a 90-degree rotation, so this is
# where the matcher's choice of orientation becomes observable. No wraps, so a LINE/LINE mesh has
# exactly the embeddings the grid allows and nothing more.
#
#   100 101 | 102 103
#   104 105 | 106 107
#   108 109 | 110 111
#   112 113 | 114 115
#
#   host of each ASIC:
#   h0 h0 h1 h1
#   h0 h0 h1 h1
#   h0 h0 h1 h1
#   h0 h0 h1 h1
#
# Every ASIC gets its own (tray_id, asic_location) = (row+1, col+1) so a PGD can name individual
# chips and pinnings stay injective. Links carry 2 channels and are marked non-local exactly when
# they cross a host boundary. Channels 0/1 run along a row, 2/3 along a column.
target_device_type: 0
